// How this app gets onto the internet (PLAN 17.16.2).
//
// The live copy is https://pelonot.showered.workers.dev — a Cloudflare Worker
// serving these files as static assets, which is why `/link.html` answers a 307
// to `/link` (the host trims `.html`, measured in 17.16).
//
// **This file is not how the site is deployed.** 17.16.2 is answered: Cloudflare
// watches the repository, so `git push` is the deploy — no build step, no
// invocation of this config. It is kept as a manual fallback, and the `name`
// below is taken from the live URL so running it would update that Worker rather
// than standing up a second one. It has never been run from this repository.
//
// One thing neither route explains: `config.js` is git-ignored and untracked,
// and the host serves it anyway. A push cannot be carrying it, so something on
// the hosting side does — which is why 17.16.3's key form cannot be moved from
// here.
//
// It changes nothing about 17.1: there is still no build step, nothing to
// install to *run* the app, and the Gradle build cannot see any of this. A
// deploy tool is not a toolchain — the page still opens from `file://`.
//
//     git push                         # the deploy
//     ./web/check-deployed.sh          # the part that actually settles it
//
// `config.js` is git-ignored and is uploaded from the working copy, which is
// deliberate and is the same decision as 17.14: the endpoint and its
// publishable key belong to whoever is hosting, not to this repository.
{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/main/packages/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "pelonot",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-15",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./"
  }
}
